# counter harness. One force call is one minhocao POSDATA evaluated by lennard_jones.
# Positions cross the socket in Bohr and return as Hartree and Ha/Bohr with FLAME Bohr_Ang and Ha_eV.
# The cluster is translated to the centre of a 1e7 Angstrom cell. The potential has no periodic images.
# ioput is the documented minhocao start 1.d-2 5.d2 1.d5. earr tolerances are 2.d-3 1.d-1.
# Local optimisation is the code default FIRE tolerance 2.d-4 Ha/Bohr.
# GEOFIREDTINIT 1.d-9 and GEOFIREDTMIN 1.d-12 replace the code defaults 10 and 1. Pairs in this archive sit near 0.02 sigma, and the default first step moves those atoms by more than the cell.
# No energy_above_minimum is stated. partial is true and the row is not ranked. A Cambridge reference ends the search at that energy plus 0.001. reference_bound marks a start that reached it. force_calls is that count. The start is not a ranked success.
# minhocao on the lj75 coordinate archive. ioput, earr tolerances, fingerprint, seed, and the FIRE force tolerance match flame/lj38-minhocao. GEOFIREDTINIT is 1.d-9 and GEOFIREDTMIN is 1.d-12. The code defaults are 10 and 1. Pairs in this archive sit near 0.02 sigma, and the default first step moves those atoms by more than the cell. The problem file does not state energy_above_minimum, so the row stays partial and is not ranked. The search ends at the Cambridge minimum -397.492331 plus 0.001. reference_bound marks a start that reached that energy, and force_calls is the harness count at that point.
